How object talk to one another?

Object form a network.
Understand object relationships (Network).

Weakest-------> Strongest:

1. Dependency (Uses-a)
2. Association (Linked-to)
3. Aggregation (Has-a : whole-part)
4. Composition (Owns-a : strong whole-part)
5. Inheritance (Is-a)

1. Dependency (Uses- A):- calculator + you.
Class A uses class B -> temporary reference.
Method finish executing -> relationship over.

2. Association (Linked-to): Doctor + Patient
Class A, Class B -> connected object-> independent lifetimes and no ownership.

3. Aggregation (Has A: Loose Ownership):-

Class A owns class B but B can exist independently of A. Class A -> destroyed , class B lives on.
-> Department and a professor.

4. Composition (Has A : strict ownership)
Class A owns class B and B can't exist independently of A.
-> class A destroy---> class B destroy.

House and its room.
-> create object B inside class A.

5. Generalization and Realization (is-A)

Generalization-> Inheritance
class A is specialized type of class B.

Realization-> Interface implementation.
class A agrees to implement the exact contract(blueprint) defined by interface B.

# Notation used in UML Diagram:-    

Relationship   │ UML Arrow Style             │ Meaning
───────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────
Dependency     │ ── ── ── ─► (Dashed Open)    │ A temporarily uses B
Association    │ ──────────► (Solid Open)     │ A is linked to B
Aggregation    │ ◇────────── (Clear Diamond)  │ A has B (B can live without A)
Composition    │ ◆────────── (Filled Diamond) │ A owns B (B dies if A dies)
Inheritance    │ ──────────▷ (Solid Triangle) │ A is a specialized subclass of B
Realization    │ ── ── ── ─▷ (Dashed Triangle)│ A implements interface B


Aggregation-> pointer.
Composition-> direct object.





